{#
  The person edit form — the Twig counterpart of
  module/Schoenstatt/view/schoenstatt/persons/edit.phtml and its fields-partial.phtml,
  which still render this page wherever laminas is the front controller. The tenth and
  last of the entity edit forms.

  Field order is that partial's, in its order, and should be changed in both or neither:
  the two renderings are live at the same time on different front controllers, and a
  moderator who edits a person through one and then the other should not see the form
  rearrange itself.

  ## Four things no earlier form in the batch needed

  - **`tel` inputs.** `cellPhone` and `phone1`–`phone3` are `SionModel\Form\Element\Phone`,
    a plain element declaring `type="tel"`. `cellPhone` is also the one field paired with
    another inside a hand-built `form-group`, so its WhatsApp checkbox sits beside it
    rather than in a row of its own.
  - **A collapse driven by a field's value.** `automaticTitle` is a checkbox whose state
    decides whether the `manualTitle` group is expanded, and the partial sets
    `aria-expanded` on the checkbox itself to match. `== 0` is the partial's comparison and
    is reproduced exactly — under PHP 8 that is true for `0`, `'0'`, `false` and `null` and
    false for `''`, and the .phtml runs on the same PHP.
  - **A title built from the record.** `<title>` is `Edit <name>`, not a fixed string:
    laminas disables the headTitle translator and inserts the person's name into a
    translated `Edit %s`. `page_title_translate = false` is this layout's equivalent — the
    name must not be run through the translator, or a person called "Home" would come out
    as the navigation label.
  - **A delete-confirmation modal**, the second in the batch after `assignment-edit`. It is
    gated on `route/persons/person/delete`, a different permission from the one that let
    the visitor reach this page, and both the trigger button and the modal sit inside that
    gate — a button that opens a modal that posts to a 403 would be worse than no button.

  ## `nameDay` is deliberately not rendered, and deliberately still posted

  The name-day field is on its way out with its database column, so it is not reproduced
  as the pair of selects the partial builds. **It is still round-tripped through three
  hidden inputs, and that is not optional.** `nameDay` is on the form's input filter, so
  omitting it entirely does not mean "leave it alone": `getData()` answers `nameDay => null`
  for an absent field, and `updateEntity()` writes that null over the stored value. Measured
  2026-08-14 — 130 of the capsule's 325 persons have a name day, and every one of them would
  have been erased the first time a moderator saved their record.

  The hidden values reproduce the stored date exactly (verified: `1900-03-19` in, the same
  DateTime out) and `1900` is the year the partial hardcodes too. When the column goes, these
  three lines and the form element go with it.

  **The field rows live in `schoenstatt/_person-fields.html.twig` now**, shared with the create
  form so that a field cannot be added to one surface and quietly forgotten on the
  other. What stays in this file is what edit.phtml keeps outside its own partial —
  which is not the same set for every entity, and is the detail worth checking before
  moving anything across the boundary.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{#
  Set before any block, so the layout sees them: a child template's top-level code runs
  before the parent renders.
#}
{#
  Reassigning `page_title` onto itself: the route declares the translatable string
  `Edit %s`, exactly as the other nine declare theirs, and this only translates it and
  drops the name in. Keeping the literal in the route declaration rather than here is what
  keeps `config/symfony/routes.php` readable as the inventory of page titles.

  Guarded on `person_name` because `person-create.html.twig` extends this file, and a
  child's top-level code runs *before* the parent's — so the create page cannot override
  this by assigning first. There is no record on a create and therefore no name; its title
  is the route's string, translated and used as it stands.
#}
{% set page_title = person_name is defined
    ? translate(page_title)|format(person_name)
    : translate(page_title) %}
{% set page_title_translate = false %}

{#
  The two assets fields-partial.phtml appends. Note the script carries **no language
  suffix**, unlike the book/text/publication bundles — `gen-schoenstatt-person-edit.js`
  contains no jQuery-validate locale strings.
#}
{% block page_stylesheets %}
        <link href="/css/gen-selectize-jquery-ui.css" media="screen" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
        <script src="/js/gen-schoenstatt-person-edit.js"></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
{#
  `Edit Person Info` in the heading, not the `Edit %s` that goes in <title>. Two different
  strings in the original, and the lead paragraph beneath carries the name.
#}
<h1>{{ translate('Edit Person Info') }}</h1>
<p class="lead">{{ person_name }}</p>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('schoenstatt/_person-fields.html.twig') }}
{#
  Whitespace-controlled on purpose. edit.phtml echoes the submit, then `&nbsp;`, then the
  button with nothing between them; a newline here reaches the page as a second space
  beside the entity, which is a byte difference for no reason.
#}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{%- if delete_action is not empty and is_allowed('route/persons/person/delete') -%}
&nbsp;{{ form_button(form.get('delete')) }}
{%- endif %}
{{ form_close() }}
{% if delete_action is not empty and is_allowed('route/persons/person/delete') %}
<!-- Modal -->
<div class="modal fade bs-example-modal-sm" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="mySmallModalLabel">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-sm">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
        <h4 class="modal-title">{{ translate('Careful') }}...</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>{{ translate("Only delete a person if he/she was created by mistake!
        		If you wish change the person in charge, simply set an \"End Date\" in the past
        		and create a new assignment.") }}</p>
{{ form_open(delete_form, delete_action) }}
{{ form_row(delete_form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(delete_form.get('submit')) -}}
&nbsp;{{ form_button(delete_form.get('cancel')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block inline_scripts %}
{#
  The selectize calls, in the partial's order — it builds the script in two pieces, the
  contact block's first and the tag pickers' after the Personal/Private sections, then
  emits them as one `$(function () { … })`.
#}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}">
$(function () {
$("select[name='country']").selectize({
    create: false,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='spousePersonId']").selectize({
    create: false,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='phone1Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='phone2Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='phone3Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='url1Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='url2Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
$("select[name='url3Label']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});

$("select[name='personTags[]']").selectize({
    create: true
});
$("select[name='adminTags[]']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});

});
</script>
{% endblock %}
